XML TO CSV
----------
Description: Transforms XML data into a flat CSV format.

config :  (General, Processing)

General :  Name

Processing :

BASIC ELEMENTS (TV)

Path to Source Element in XML (ET) :
-> Enter the xpath of record identifier


Field Separator in CSV (DD) : (colon, comma, dot, pipe , semicolon, space , tab)
-> Enter field separator in csv

CSV Header (DD) :  (None, XML Based , XSD annotation based)
-> Select how to include the field names as headers in the converted CSV file.
   None: To skip adding headers
   XML based: To use an XML element for header name.
   XSD annotation based: To use <xsd:documentation> tag inside xsd element's <xsd:annotation> tag for header name.
   Note.

   XML Schema (select) : (only if you select CSV Header as XSD annotation based)
   -> Define the XML schema path or choose Select to upload the XML schema from your local file system by choosing Upload from File System.
      You can also enter ${header.headername} or ${property.propertyname} to read the path dynamically from a header or a property. To fetch details from partner directory, use syntax pd: <header_name>.

   PARENT ELEMENT (TV)

  Include Parent Element (CD) :
  -> Select this checkbox if you want to include the parent element of the XML file in CSV file

  Path to Parent Element (ET) :
  ->Enter the Xpath of master record identifier

  Include Attribute Values (CD) :
  -> include attribute values

















